<section>
    <h2>Emergency use and delivery limits</h2>
    <p>Provide truthful information to the best of your knowledge. Do not knowingly create false, prank, threatening, or duplicate emergencies. A reference code confirms the application received a record; acknowledgment confirms a recorded response action. Neither guarantees official dispatch, rescue arrival, or a particular response time.</p>
    <p>Online reporting needs a working connection and the required verification/location steps. For local LoRa reporting, remain near a powered node; forwarding depends on radio reachability, power, and a route to NODE_1. Delivery to the hosted website also needs the gateway's server connection. A saved draft or locally queued message is not proof of website delivery.</p>
    <p>If someone is in immediate danger and the app cannot complete a report, contact available local emergency services or seek nearby assistance. Do not delay urgent help while waiting for an app notification.</p>
</section>
<section>
    <h2>Your account and submitted material</h2>
    <p>Keep your password private, use your own permitted account, and sign out on shared devices. Do not impersonate another person, access another user's records, share protected evidence without authority, or bypass verification/security controls. Administrators may restrict access when misuse is identified; contact the operator if you believe a restriction is incorrect.</p>
    <p>Submit only information and media you are permitted to share for the reporting purpose. Avoid unnecessary private details or graphic content unrelated to the incident. Submission permits handling needed for incident review and coordination under the applicable processing basis; it does not transfer ownership or authorize unrelated publication, advertising, or model training.</p>
</section>
<section>
    <h2>AI and human review</h2>
    <p>The experimental description classifier can be wrong or abstain. Its class scores are not medical findings. Authorized humans review available information and decide how to record severity and response status. Do not treat a Minor suggestion as medical clearance, a Critical suggestion as certified death, or an AI result as permission to act outside your role.</p>
</section>
<section>
    <h2>Availability and responsible access</h2>
    <p>This prototype may be interrupted by server, device, network, radio, power, or verification-service failures. Features can be corrected or updated. Do not overload the service, introduce malicious files, misuse open field-node access, or interfere with another person's emergency report.</p>
    <p>No outcome or uninterrupted availability is promised. Nothing in these terms removes rights or responsibilities that cannot lawfully be excluded. The operator's obligations and any dispute are subject to applicable Philippine law; this page does not create immunity from negligent or unlawful conduct.</p>
</section>
